        "descriptions": [
            {
                "value": "This dataset contains time-resolved path gain measurements of line-of-sight (LOS) wireless communication links at 60 GHz and 300 GHz. The measurements capture the temporal evolution of the channel while a moving person intermittently obstructs the direct propagation path, causing shadowing and blockage effects. The recorded data provide insight into the dynamics of human-induced attenuation and channel variations in millimeter-wave and sub-THz frequency bands. These measurements can be used to analyze blockage characteristics, evaluate channel models, and support the design and performance assessment of future high-frequency wireless communication systems.",
                "descriptionType": "Abstract",
                "lang": "en"
            }
        ],
